@page "/experiments"

<PageTitle>Experiments · Denny Kim</PageTitle>

<div class="pf-hero">
    <h1>Experiments</h1>
    <p>UX explorations that don't fit in the component workshop yet. Each one starts as a question, gets a working prototype, and either graduates into the library or teaches something and retires.</p>
</div>

<div class="pf-section">
    <div class="pf-cards">
        <div class="pf-card">
            <span class="pf-tag">Exploration</span>
            <h3>Agentic commerce</h3>
            <p>What does a parts storefront look like when an AI agent does the shopping? Delegated fitment verification, agent-readable product data, and the UX of supervising instead of clicking.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pf-card">
            <span class="pf-tag">Exploration</span>
            <h3>Conversational fitment</h3>
            <p>"I need brakes for my 2024 XC40" — a chatbot that resolves vehicle, category, and qualifier questions into a real fitment, then hands off to the existing picker components.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pf-card">
            <span class="pf-tag">Exploration</span>
            <h3>Assembly diagram ↔ parts table</h3>
            <p>The classic OEM pattern: click a callout on the diagram, highlight the row in the parts table. Prototyping the interaction details — hover states, mobile behavior, supersession display.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pf-card">
            <span class="pf-tag">Exploration</span>
            <h3>Checkout confidence</h3>
            <p>Fitment guarantee messaging, delivery-vs-pickup as a first-class choice, and price-stack clarity at the moment of commitment.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
